{"title":"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 CEMC Fermat #8</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 CEMC Pascal #13</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Corina had added the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> correctly, the answer would have been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. By mistake, she subtracted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Her answer was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2bf29dad4b776f587bdef40e74a8031268c4184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can set up equations using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d36190f5b06a311b104e285f351ca3d322397a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P + Q = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/381877f22e047ad8a61fb2fffe33dacc2a67d7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P - Q = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>From the second equation, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca6b7735c48b4d2fdb35b283bc2fa0b12e87efa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 4 + Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a61eb7f0a5f68a826f302430109b647b47504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = P - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a61eb7f0a5f68a826f302430109b647b47504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = P - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> into the first equation, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/306564100901554c9b433ad2e3f8659b6e7678fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P + P - 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/4300279f3ce7e52fef58b2f1bd921f49f6df5b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2P - 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7fc0901294d4001838a6b04dfd5064bf1a88deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2P = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bb6f66f7ed0cc739b420a7a609312f3fbc3e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"106\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>We can also check our answer:\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d9351269e0df082c943107fdb08c8d09995e418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/9/8a9f45433d1e19ba56b92115d997b323e39a6ec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = P - 4 = 10 - 4 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging this into the equations, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46358d1eb17b4d65bc00cc217dcb28eaf81c8e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 6 = 16 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c836de6535e9902902c7fa901b10a152662ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 6 = 4 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This works out, so our answer for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is correct. \n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use elimination to solve the equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d36190f5b06a311b104e285f351ca3d322397a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P + Q = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/381877f22e047ad8a61fb2fffe33dacc2a67d7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P - Q = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can notice one equation has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> while the other has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c2b8678b98ff3fac7e984aa880e2416d309340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, so we can add them:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2408528f60edb4e77ae5a69918771b7d75bcc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P + Q + P - Q = 16 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying both sides, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7fc0901294d4001838a6b04dfd5064bf1a88deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2P = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bb6f66f7ed0cc739b420a7a609312f3fbc3e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"106\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal\">2006 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"CEMC Pascal\">CEMC Pascal</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat\">2006 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Probl